WEBVTT

00:27.470 --> 00:29.470
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

01:41.500 --> 01:45.670
EPISODE 52: EACH RESPECTIVE ROLES
Well, let's talk about the festival later.

01:45.670 --> 01:49.210
Soei, have there been any changes
in our monster ecosystem?

01:49.530 --> 01:53.660
I had my Body Doubles
survey the surrounding areas,

01:53.660 --> 01:56.390
but I did not discover anything
particularly problematic.

01:56.390 --> 01:57.310
I see.

01:57.310 --> 01:58.680
If I had to name one...

02:03.110 --> 02:07.270
There was a Sword Grizzly wreaking havoc
in the northwestern area of the forest...

02:10.530 --> 02:11.900
So I safely dispatched it.

02:11.900 --> 02:12.790
Good.

02:12.790 --> 02:14.660
So there was nothing
to worry about.

02:14.660 --> 02:15.660
Report.

02:15.660 --> 02:18.760
A Sword Grizzly is equivalent
to an A-minus rank,

02:18.760 --> 02:20.540
similar to a Knight Spider.

02:20.540 --> 02:21.540
What?!

02:21.540 --> 02:25.830
Isn't that a monster regular adventurers
would have a hard time to deal with?

02:25.830 --> 02:26.540
Yes, sir.

02:26.540 --> 02:27.790
Is that for real?

02:27.790 --> 02:31.710
Then it'd be dangerous to deploy
anyone new with them around.

02:31.710 --> 02:35.490
It wouldn't be a problem.
You just spoil them too much, anyway.

02:35.490 --> 02:39.060
Guys like us can't afford to let our guard
down against a monster like that, okay?

02:39.060 --> 02:42.680
Then you just have to ask
for harder training.

02:42.680 --> 02:43.810
He's correct.

02:43.810 --> 02:44.890
You demon!

02:45.650 --> 02:47.150
Yes, I am.

02:49.570 --> 02:53.400
But well, training Gobta
and his team is a good thing.

02:53.400 --> 02:56.360
Anyway, the problem is
the emerging monsters.

02:56.360 --> 02:58.620
It'd be too late if we start
having casualties.

02:58.620 --> 03:01.080
We need something
to deal with that.

03:01.080 --> 03:05.080
In that case, why don't we place
Anti-Magic Barrier over the highways?

03:05.670 --> 03:07.460
Anti-Magic Barrier?

03:07.460 --> 03:09.920
Rimuru, it's complete.

03:09.920 --> 03:14.720
The prototype for a fully automatic
magic generator that can produce barrier!

03:15.220 --> 03:17.970
I knew you had been working
on something in secret,

03:17.970 --> 03:20.470
but a fully automatic magic generator?

03:20.470 --> 03:23.930
It automatically keeps
the magic we insert running.

03:23.930 --> 03:26.100
A revolutionary magic device.

03:26.600 --> 03:28.980
Like a Rune magic?

03:29.480 --> 03:33.480
Yes, but it has better performance
and can operate on a much larger scale.

03:33.820 --> 03:39.370
We couldn't help much during
the barrier crisis time, after all.

03:39.370 --> 03:41.490
So we wanted to make up for it.

03:41.490 --> 03:45.750
They managed to create a working
model in such a short time?

03:46.100 --> 03:48.250
They're such geniuses!

03:48.250 --> 03:52.250
Kurobe and I lend them our hand
during our spare time.

03:53.740 --> 03:56.380
I was helping out, too.

03:57.470 --> 04:00.640
Then it is a culmination
of Tempest's magic tech!

04:02.560 --> 04:08.100
As a land of monsters, Tempest has
a high density of magicules in the air.

04:08.100 --> 04:12.190
So I have been thinking of a way
to take advantage of it.

04:12.560 --> 04:19.070
This automatic magic generator makes use of
surrounding magicules from the atmosphere.

04:19.410 --> 04:22.450
So we can erect
an Anti-Magic Barrier with this?

04:22.450 --> 04:23.370
Yes.

04:23.370 --> 04:27.040
However,
that's not the only good thing about it.

04:27.710 --> 04:31.710
But the Anti-Magic Barrier is meant
to prevent monsters from coming in, right?

04:31.710 --> 04:33.840
What else can we gain from it?

04:35.130 --> 04:37.220
Get this, Rimuru!

04:37.640 --> 04:42.470
It actually has a mechanism
that accumulates magicules!

04:42.470 --> 04:48.560
We can use this to lower
the density of magicules in the air!

04:48.560 --> 04:53.150
Whoa! That's exactly the problem
we were trying to solve!

04:53.150 --> 04:55.980
There you have it, Great Rimuru.

04:55.980 --> 04:59.450
But it is not without its drawbacks.

04:59.450 --> 05:03.870
It requires a certain level of magicule density,
otherwise it's too inefficient.

05:04.370 --> 05:08.000
But we wouldn't have to worry
about that around this town.

05:08.000 --> 05:09.580
In fact, I couldn't ask for more!

05:10.160 --> 05:14.790
So basically this device will
suck magicules from the air

05:14.790 --> 05:18.210
and automatically keep
an Anti-Magic Barrier up for us?

05:18.210 --> 05:20.930
Well, we could use it like that.

05:20.930 --> 05:24.300
But then the barrier will be gone
once its internal magicule runs out.

05:24.300 --> 05:28.560
So we made it
so it can refill its fuel.

05:28.560 --> 05:29.910
Fuel?

05:29.910 --> 05:32.600
The crystallization of magicules
it gathered from the air.

05:32.600 --> 05:34.980
In other words, a magicrystal.

05:36.360 --> 05:42.740
Magicstone aside, won't it be inefficient
to use magicrystal for fuel as is?

05:42.740 --> 05:43.820
Answer.

05:43.820 --> 05:48.740
Converting magicrystal into magic energy
would waste 90 percent of its magicule.

05:48.740 --> 05:54.580
That's right, but we have the Rune magic
you made for us.

05:54.580 --> 05:55.880
Oh, I see!

05:56.200 --> 05:59.510
With Rune magic that decreases
consumption to a minimum,

05:59.510 --> 06:02.720
we can still get the desired effects
even with just 10 percent of it.

06:02.720 --> 06:07.100
And it's not like the "wasted"
magicules will be gone forever.

06:07.100 --> 06:09.430
It will be back,
and we could use it again!

06:09.770 --> 06:13.940
That means we can achieve
a perpetual motion!

06:14.340 --> 06:16.060
If the magicule density decreases,

06:16.060 --> 06:18.860
there will be fewer monsters
and Mystic Beast popping out.

06:18.860 --> 06:21.490
That means there would be
fewer strong monsters being born

06:21.490 --> 06:23.990
that might pose trouble for Gobta's team!

06:23.990 --> 06:26.740
This is a marvelous invention!

06:27.140 --> 06:29.910
It matches our nation's
unique traits perfectly!

06:30.620 --> 06:35.000
Furthermore, it could cast more than
just an Anti-Magic Barrier!

06:36.850 --> 06:39.920
There's a limit on the type of magic
it could cast, but...

06:43.590 --> 06:45.130
Let me help.

06:46.390 --> 06:50.390
By changing the magic board
that has magic formula engraved on it,

06:50.390 --> 06:53.640
we could activate
a different kind of magic.

06:55.330 --> 06:57.940
It's like a record player!

06:58.430 --> 07:03.440
I had no idea they'd leverage my vague
story into something magical like this!

07:03.870 --> 07:08.410
If we could miniaturize it,
maybe we could even make them portable.

07:08.410 --> 07:13.410
Or perhaps make it larger
for tactical-level magic deployment?

07:15.330 --> 07:20.340
Now, allow me to propose
an idea on how to use it.

07:20.800 --> 07:27.180
First, we install these devices
evenly spaced across the highways

07:27.180 --> 07:29.510
and activate the Anti-Magic Barrier.

07:29.510 --> 07:34.310
With high enough magicule density,
there's no need to charge or replace its fuel.

07:34.890 --> 07:39.060
We just have to simply check daily
to see if the barrier is still working.

07:39.060 --> 07:42.250
I see. You really thought this one up.

07:42.250 --> 07:45.280
It's easy to use and can be used
for a wide variety of functions.

07:45.280 --> 07:48.570
So what about the magic formula board
for the barrier?

07:50.570 --> 07:53.080
Dold's already got it done.

07:53.490 --> 07:56.580
We already asked Kurobe to work out
on the manufacturing,

07:56.580 --> 07:58.750
so all left is for your permission.

07:58.750 --> 08:00.210
Yes.

08:00.210 --> 08:01.460
I see.

08:01.460 --> 08:04.800
Then can I have you in charge
of this project for us, Vesta?

08:04.800 --> 08:09.300
I've been holding fewer classes now,
so I would love to take this job on.

08:09.970 --> 08:12.350
All right.
I want you to begin tomorrow.

08:12.350 --> 08:14.310
Leave it to me, sir.

08:14.310 --> 08:15.950
This is pretty heavy.

08:15.950 --> 08:18.560
You could leave the installation work to us.

08:18.560 --> 08:21.110
That would be much appreciated, Mr. Geld.

08:24.020 --> 08:28.610
So once that is complete,
I can release as much aura as I desire?

08:30.490 --> 08:34.580
No, you can't! If you do that,
the majority of people here will die!

08:36.330 --> 08:41.500
But I have been holding it in for so long,
it's actually starting to wear me ou—

08:41.500 --> 08:42.960
Deal with it.

08:42.960 --> 08:43.840
Sob.

08:44.380 --> 08:47.920
Besides, Rimuru!
Why are you okay?

08:47.920 --> 08:51.590
Me? I just shove it all in my Stomach.

08:52.050 --> 08:55.770
All the time, since Rigurd pointed it out.

08:56.220 --> 08:59.480
My magicule boosted after
I ascended to Demon Lord,

08:59.480 --> 09:03.440
but at the same time,
my Predator evolved into Beelzebub,

09:03.440 --> 09:06.780
which vastly expanded
my Stomach storage.

09:06.780 --> 09:11.610
Thanks to that, I had no desire
to unleash my magicule at all.

09:11.610 --> 09:13.490
However, Great Rimuru, if I may.

09:13.490 --> 09:15.470
For an individual such as Veldora,

09:15.470 --> 09:19.540
It is insanely difficult
to completely suppress their aura.

09:19.540 --> 09:23.880
Even Sir Benimaru and his group
are leaking out a tiny amount of it.

09:23.880 --> 09:27.760
Yes! You are an observant demon,
aren't you, Diablo?

09:27.760 --> 09:32.220
Lord Veldora has an enormous amount
of magicule in him,

09:32.220 --> 09:35.300
so keeping it all within himself
requires a lot of effort.

09:35.300 --> 09:37.010
Is that true, Veldora?

09:37.010 --> 09:42.140
Yes, it is! That's why I want to
go blow it up somewhere!

09:42.140 --> 09:44.690
If he were to actually
blow it up somewhere,

09:44.690 --> 09:47.690
that whole area would be a death zone.

09:47.690 --> 09:53.570
It might spawn freaky powerful monsters
or even another Charybdis-level horror.

09:53.570 --> 09:55.660
It'll be a catastrophe, literally.

09:56.090 --> 10:00.290
All right. I'll think about that,
so hold it in for a while longer, okay?

10:00.290 --> 10:01.370
Very well!

10:01.370 --> 10:04.750
I can manage that well enough,
but try to be quick about it!

10:05.170 --> 10:06.340
Good grief.

10:06.340 --> 10:09.510
Here I thought we just solved
the magicule-density problem,

10:09.510 --> 10:11.840
but now we have an even
bigger problem to deal with.

10:11.840 --> 10:14.300
Here. Enjoy.

10:14.300 --> 10:17.600
No one human would know just
what life's gonna throw at you.

10:17.600 --> 10:20.310
I'm a slime, though.

10:26.730 --> 10:29.980
Well, now that we're done
with all the reports...

10:32.650 --> 10:33.520
Here.

10:35.490 --> 10:37.120
Wh-What is this?

10:37.450 --> 10:40.160
I want to leave this
construction job to you.

10:40.160 --> 10:44.120
This is the castle for Milim I've been
crafting here and there in my spare time.

10:44.120 --> 10:47.790
I believe you're up to the task.

10:47.790 --> 10:49.800
What do you think?
Are you up for it?

10:50.500 --> 10:51.910
Great Rimuru...

10:52.300 --> 10:55.050
Ah, did I put too much pressure on him?

10:56.800 --> 10:58.760
Leave it to us, Rimuru.

10:58.760 --> 11:01.430
I'll go there and give Geld
all the backup he needs.

11:02.020 --> 11:03.890
We'll take Myrd along, too,

11:03.890 --> 11:08.190
so you can have him handle
your little city planning project, right?

11:09.270 --> 11:11.780
With Kaijin's help,
I'm sure it'll be okay.

11:11.780 --> 11:12.970
This is good.

11:13.440 --> 11:17.730
You blow away your small worries
by completing one big challenge.

11:18.450 --> 11:21.120
Geld, I'm sure you'll be fine.

11:21.120 --> 11:23.830
But of course, if you need any help,
I'm all ears.

11:23.830 --> 11:25.710
Just take it easy, okay?

11:25.710 --> 11:30.460
B-But what if I fail at a job
as large as this one?

11:30.460 --> 11:32.340
It's fine! It's fine!

11:32.340 --> 11:35.840
Even if you do, that's still gonna
be a vital experience for you.

11:35.840 --> 11:39.300
At worst, we just have to pay
the cost of a typical city.

11:39.300 --> 11:40.720
We can always earn it back.

11:40.720 --> 11:44.560
Yeah! He's right!
I mean, look at me! Last time—

11:44.560 --> 11:45.590
Hm?

11:47.180 --> 11:48.940
Last time you did what?

11:48.940 --> 11:52.020
Meet me again at my office later
to tell me in detail.

11:52.020 --> 11:54.610
What?! Was this whole
thing a trap for me?!

11:58.030 --> 12:00.370
Thank you, Great Rimuru.

12:00.370 --> 12:03.990
I suppose I was letting myself
overwhelmed by small things.

12:04.540 --> 12:08.790
Please, allow me
to take on this large job!

12:08.790 --> 12:10.380
Good to hear.
You've got the job!

12:12.210 --> 12:14.380
Why does he get all the attention?

12:14.380 --> 12:16.380
It's the right person
for the right place.

12:16.380 --> 12:18.510
You have your own work, don't you?

12:18.510 --> 12:19.640
Ah, yes! Cooking!

12:19.640 --> 12:20.640
No, it's not!

12:20.640 --> 12:25.640
W-Well, there are actually a lot,
but I wouldn't say cooking is one of them.

12:25.640 --> 12:26.980
That's right, Shion.

12:26.980 --> 12:30.850
When I'm gone, please keep Great Rimuru
safe and sound, all right?

12:30.850 --> 12:32.020
Of course!

12:32.020 --> 12:33.210
Now then...

12:33.860 --> 12:36.370
That should cover
all of today's topics, right?

12:36.370 --> 12:38.700
Oops, I almost forgot.

12:38.700 --> 12:41.870
How was the progress on your end, Diablo?

12:41.870 --> 12:44.160
Very well.
If you allow me.

12:44.910 --> 12:46.910
First, as for Sir Youm...

12:47.580 --> 12:51.000
Negotiating directly with the royalty
would prove a challenge for him.

12:51.460 --> 12:55.380
So I'm having Edmaris
beat all the manners into him.

12:56.460 --> 12:58.470
Must be hard for him...

12:58.970 --> 13:00.930
Depending on how things worked out,

13:00.930 --> 13:04.600
it might be interesting
to pull Edmaris into our side.

13:04.600 --> 13:06.720
That's an option, yeah.

13:06.720 --> 13:09.690
As for his younger brother,
the new king Edward...

13:09.690 --> 13:12.980
As we expect, he's been making
some moves behind the scenes.

13:12.980 --> 13:17.890
But wouldn't it take several months to
regroup his forces and take real action?

13:19.110 --> 13:21.080
I would like to speed up this process,

13:21.080 --> 13:23.370
so I am taking measures
to hasten the preparation.

13:23.370 --> 13:26.660
Huh? Then how about us?
Don't we also need time to prepare?

13:26.660 --> 13:28.040
No problems there.

13:28.040 --> 13:31.620
I have Sir Benimaru organize the forces
we will deploy when the time is right.

13:31.620 --> 13:33.870
Yes, we are all set to go.

13:33.870 --> 13:37.370
One force will operate in the public,
and another will operate in the shadows.

13:37.370 --> 13:39.260
Both are ready for action.

13:39.680 --> 13:43.140
In fact, many were so eager to participate
that it's hard to select them.

13:43.140 --> 13:44.510
I-I see...

13:44.510 --> 13:46.510
This isn't a picnic trip, though.

13:46.510 --> 13:47.970
Also...

13:47.970 --> 13:50.430
I wouldn't exactly call this
a problem, but...

13:50.430 --> 13:51.470
What is it?

13:51.470 --> 13:54.020
Reyhiem has yet to return.

13:54.380 --> 13:55.940
He hasn't?

13:56.270 --> 13:58.610
He went to deliver my message, right?

13:58.610 --> 14:01.400
Did he not make it or something?

14:01.400 --> 14:04.840
No, I had my men to
take him directly

14:04.840 --> 14:08.700
to the Engrassia capital with
the crystal ball in his hand.

14:09.240 --> 14:11.710
As there is a barrier
surrounding the capital,

14:11.710 --> 14:14.080
none of my men was able
to infiltrate the area,

14:14.080 --> 14:18.090
but they confirmed
that he had arrived safely in the city.

14:18.090 --> 14:19.590
Engrassia?

14:20.060 --> 14:22.470
There is a special transport gate there

14:22.470 --> 14:26.760
that leads directly to
the Holy Empire of Lubelius,

14:26.760 --> 14:29.970
so I had Reyhiem use that to get
to the Church headquarters.

14:29.970 --> 14:31.180
Report.

14:31.180 --> 14:34.230
Transport gate is a magic
circle that allows you

14:34.230 --> 14:37.980
to instantly teleport between two points
by crossing a special dimension.

14:38.350 --> 14:41.990
I should be briefed on his return.

14:41.990 --> 14:45.240
And you have not received any report?

14:45.580 --> 14:48.160
Did they kill him to shut him up, maybe?

14:48.160 --> 14:52.040
No, I have not detected
any such thing as of yet.

14:52.040 --> 14:55.710
My Tempter skill can seize
the soul of anyone

14:55.710 --> 14:58.880
it has thrall over
the moment they die.

14:58.880 --> 15:01.420
Well, if he's still alive, then fine.

15:01.420 --> 15:04.880
As long as they didn't kill him
and blame us for it, it's all good.

15:05.310 --> 15:07.010
Still, what a problem.

15:07.010 --> 15:10.680
We know far too little to
accurately grasp the situation.

15:10.680 --> 15:12.470
My apologies.

15:12.470 --> 15:15.270
Attempting to infiltrate Lubelius
would be too dangerous...

15:15.270 --> 15:19.310
Oh, no, no, you're fine!
Moreover, Hinata is also there.

15:19.310 --> 15:21.780
Pushing yourself too hard
won't do us any good.

15:22.690 --> 15:24.530
Hinata Sakaguchi...

15:24.990 --> 15:29.700
I suggest putting the whole ruckus from
before firmly behind us in my message.

15:30.200 --> 15:32.240
I add in some little taunt, too,

15:32.240 --> 15:34.410
but hey, gotta have
some little fun, right?

15:34.910 --> 15:39.710
The most ideal outcome would be
if they choose to coexist with us.

15:40.250 --> 15:45.920
Diablo's plans should work as long as
the Western Holy Church doesn't do anything.

15:45.920 --> 15:49.930
Personally, I would prefer to have
our dispute firmly settled for good.

15:49.930 --> 15:56.270
We were attacked while you
were fighting the Saint Hinata.

15:56.270 --> 15:58.480
These attacks were
undoubtedly linked,

15:58.480 --> 16:00.690
and someone likely
arranged them to happen.

16:01.440 --> 16:03.320
And as if to confirm that,

16:03.320 --> 16:06.700
Clayman hinted at the presence
of someone behind the scenes...

16:06.700 --> 16:08.740
That "he," right?

16:08.740 --> 16:14.080
Yes, and we will need to consider
his upcoming moves as well.

16:14.080 --> 16:17.210
He's a foe we cannot afford
to let our guard down against.

16:17.210 --> 16:18.690
Yeah.

16:19.310 --> 16:24.220
If that guy's involved, there is a chance
that Hinata might take action, too...

16:24.880 --> 16:27.340
But something doesn't seem right to me.

16:28.130 --> 16:30.930
Am I overlooking something?

16:32.190 --> 16:35.310
Say, do you think Hinata attacked me
not of her own volition,

16:35.310 --> 16:39.190
but instead, asked to or ordered to
by someone?

16:40.340 --> 16:41.480
What do you mean?

16:42.900 --> 16:48.070
To be frank, I don't think Hinata
would be taking orders from anyone.

16:48.900 --> 16:51.620
You're right.

16:51.620 --> 16:54.700
If there's anyone who could order
that captain of the crusaders,

16:54.700 --> 16:56.410
that would be the god Luminus herself.

16:56.410 --> 16:58.160
God Luminus?

16:58.160 --> 16:59.670
Luminus?

16:59.670 --> 17:05.300
Everyone knows that not even
the Holy Emperor could order her around.

17:05.300 --> 17:08.090
Yeah, you see?

17:08.090 --> 17:11.430
She sure didn't listen to me at all.

17:11.820 --> 17:15.060
So there isn't anyone who could
give orders to Hinata...

17:15.560 --> 17:18.560
Then the timing was just a coincidence?

17:18.560 --> 17:21.190
There's a chance she's being led on.

17:21.600 --> 17:22.440
But...

17:22.440 --> 17:27.320
But you doubt said mastermind was
in a position to order her around?

17:27.320 --> 17:28.820
Exactly.

17:28.820 --> 17:34.160
This mastermind drove Falmuth to action,
manipulated Demon Lord Clayman,

17:34.160 --> 17:36.740
and tried to destroy our nation.

17:36.740 --> 17:41.210
But he didn't have that kind
of free control over Hinata?

17:41.610 --> 17:44.250
Does that mean you don't think
the Western Holy Church

17:44.250 --> 17:47.670
will make any move at the moment,
Great Rimuru?

17:47.670 --> 17:49.720
That's the thing.

17:50.080 --> 17:54.510
I told her loud and clear that
I had no intention of being her enemy.

17:54.510 --> 17:57.930
And Hinata couldn't be
stupid enough to know that

17:57.930 --> 18:00.850
and still want to take on Tempest
which has me and Veldora in it.

18:01.560 --> 18:04.350
Hinata said we were a hindrance to her.

18:04.350 --> 18:08.150
And that is because the teachings
of the Holy Church, the Luminism,

18:08.150 --> 18:10.990
dictate that life alongside
monsters is unacceptable.

18:10.990 --> 18:13.990
But perhaps that's not
all there is behind it...

18:13.990 --> 18:15.030
Report.

18:15.030 --> 18:18.370
There is an increased possibility
that multiple motives are in place.

18:18.870 --> 18:21.810
All these events are interconnected.

18:21.810 --> 18:26.540
However, it is estimated that they are not
all occurring by the will of a single entity.

18:26.540 --> 18:28.340
Um, which means?

18:28.340 --> 18:29.340
Answer.

18:29.340 --> 18:33.630
Considering the nations, people, factions,
and other factors involved—

18:33.630 --> 18:36.640
These goals may seem to match
one another at first glance,

18:36.640 --> 18:38.460
but it also shows several contradictions.

18:38.460 --> 18:42.020
It would be unnatural to unify everything
under the will of a single mastermind.

18:42.020 --> 18:45.480
Which means there
isn't just one mastermind.

18:45.480 --> 18:48.520
I see. Once I think of it that way,
it makes sense.

18:49.110 --> 18:51.330
We were a hindrance to Clayman.

18:51.330 --> 18:54.450
However, at the same time,
he also tried to take advantage of us.

18:54.450 --> 18:58.370
That's why he would've loved it
if Hinata and I beat each other out.

18:59.030 --> 19:02.690
As a chancellor, the Kingdom of Falmuth
also sees me as a hindrance.

19:03.120 --> 19:06.040
They should also love to see me
get taken down by Hinata.

19:06.040 --> 19:09.210
As for Hinata,
in adherence to her teaching,

19:09.210 --> 19:12.400
she couldn't ignore my existence.

19:13.090 --> 19:17.590
These three motives align
and things take a turn.

19:17.590 --> 19:24.230
As a result, I fled from Hinata,
Falmuth retreated, and Clayman died.

19:24.850 --> 19:30.150
"That man" behind the scenes must be busy
rebuilding what little forces he had left.

19:30.150 --> 19:33.650
In that state, would he still want
to fight me directly?

19:34.360 --> 19:35.320
Answer.

19:35.320 --> 19:37.660
The possibility
of taking such action is low.

19:37.660 --> 19:40.740
If the mastermind's powers
exceeded Clayman's,

19:40.740 --> 19:43.500
he would have gotten involved
well ahead of when he did.

19:43.500 --> 19:46.000
Which means, there's no reason
for him to come after me.

19:46.500 --> 19:50.710
Not like this guy in the shadows would
reveal himself now, long after the fact.

19:50.710 --> 19:51.640
Report.

19:51.640 --> 19:54.300
It must not be forgotten
that there is a high possibility

19:54.300 --> 19:57.720
multiple people working
in the background.

19:57.720 --> 19:59.020
Good point.

19:59.510 --> 20:03.350
And if there were,
whether Hinata wanted it or not,

20:03.350 --> 20:05.770
things could keep on moving forward.

20:06.640 --> 20:09.230
Perhaps, because there are
multiple interests at stake here,

20:09.230 --> 20:14.780
we should work on the assumption that
it is not solely Hinata's decision to make?

20:14.780 --> 20:16.900
Well said, Diablo.

20:17.310 --> 20:20.200
Perhaps we misunderstood this
whole situation from the start.

20:20.200 --> 20:21.580
What do you mean?

20:21.580 --> 20:26.290
Like Diablo just said, there might
be more than one "mastermind."

20:26.290 --> 20:31.130
Maybe things are like this because their
interests are conflicting with one another.

20:31.130 --> 20:33.880
I see. Spectacular theory, Great Rimuru.

20:34.270 --> 20:38.260
And you think these multiple interests
are linked with the one Clayman spoke of?

20:38.260 --> 20:39.720
I don't know.

20:39.720 --> 20:43.680
But it is dangerous to act based on assumptions
when there's not enough info.

20:43.680 --> 20:49.020
Like, if Hinata was moving based
on obligations, not necessarily orders.

20:51.400 --> 20:55.280
In that case, I will investigate further.

20:55.280 --> 20:59.450
It was a merchant who provided Edmaris
and his ministers with their information,

20:59.450 --> 21:03.160
but thinking about it now,
that should have raised my suspicions.

21:03.160 --> 21:05.290
Hang on.
A merchant?

21:05.290 --> 21:07.250
Is something bothering you?

21:07.250 --> 21:09.530
War gets money to move around,

21:09.530 --> 21:11.790
and you always have people
trying to profit from it.

21:11.790 --> 21:18.220
Maybe those merchants are working
behind the scenes to reap some profits?

21:18.220 --> 21:19.220
I see.

21:24.180 --> 21:24.760
Shuna.

21:24.760 --> 21:27.720
Examine the account books we recovered
from Clayman's castle

21:27.720 --> 21:30.190
and see which merchants
were frequent visitors.

21:30.190 --> 21:31.270
Yes, sir.

21:31.770 --> 21:35.820
Diablo, pin down all merchants
Falmuth had ties with.

21:35.820 --> 21:37.780
At once, my lord.

21:38.310 --> 21:41.070
Benimaru, redo your selections
for Youm's reinforcements.

21:41.070 --> 21:43.450
They'll need to be prepared for anything.

21:43.450 --> 21:45.160
Yeah, leave it to me.

21:45.500 --> 21:50.330
Rigurd, we're going to hold a banger
of a festival, so get it ready.

21:50.330 --> 21:52.460
That goes without saying!

21:52.460 --> 21:55.670
Geld, just focus on your own work.

21:55.670 --> 21:56.630
Of course, sir.

21:56.630 --> 21:58.760
Hakuro, you assist Benimaru.

21:58.760 --> 21:59.460
Yes, sir.

21:59.460 --> 22:01.420
Gabiru, work with Rigurd.

22:01.420 --> 22:02.090
Roger that!

22:02.090 --> 22:05.140
And Rigur, shake down
our town's security system

22:05.140 --> 22:07.680
to be ready for all the people
that will be coming.

22:07.680 --> 22:08.810
On it!

22:09.240 --> 22:10.430
And for Shion...

22:12.190 --> 22:14.480
Um, Shion will...

22:17.020 --> 22:18.150
That!

22:18.150 --> 22:20.860
You will be my guard along with Ranga!

22:20.860 --> 22:22.700
- Yes, sir!
- Leave it to us!

22:22.700 --> 22:23.660
Master!

22:24.410 --> 22:25.910
That should do it.

22:25.910 --> 22:27.280
What about me?

22:27.280 --> 22:29.040
Oh, yeah.

22:29.040 --> 22:31.500
Veldora, you stay out of everyone's way.

22:31.500 --> 22:33.000
It shall be done!

22:33.000 --> 22:34.120
I'm worried.

22:34.670 --> 22:37.090
Oh, also. Gobta.

22:37.090 --> 22:41.030
I know you're tired,
but come see me in my office.

22:43.010 --> 22:45.260
And like that, even after
becoming a Demon Lord,

22:45.260 --> 22:49.850
our executives meeting
came to an end as usual.

23:00.940 --> 23:02.310
Sorry for the wait.

23:03.450 --> 23:05.220
Let us begin.

24:36.620 --> 24:39.190
Next time, "Two Sides Meeting."
